<Base title="AI Search Competitive Intelligence | Federica Iengo" description="A reproducible competitive intelligence benchmark for AI Search visibility, citations and retrieval.">
<p class="eyebrow">Python · AI Search · Competitive intelligence</p><h1>AI Search Competitive Intelligence</h1>
<p>A reproducible benchmark designed to compare brands across the same buyer-intent prompt set without treating a single AI answer as a ranking.</p>
<h2>Measurement model</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>Mention coverage</h3><p>Share of prompts in which each brand is explicitly mentioned.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Citation coverage</h3><p>Share of prompts for which owned or relevant third-party sources are cited.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Recommendation inclusion</h3><p>Frequency of inclusion in shortlists and recommendation contexts.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Consistency</h3><p>Stability of brand positioning across prompt families and repeated observations.</p></article></div>
<h2>Prompt families</h2><p>Category discovery · alternatives · brand-vs-brand comparison · capability/use-case · pricing/value · implementation/integration · buyer-stage recommendation.</p>
<h2>Output</h2><p>Python-generated scorecards, prompt-level evidence, source analysis, topical/entity gaps and prioritized recommendations. Raw observations remain auditable so interpretation can be challenged or reproduced.</p>
</Base>